      "writtenOn": "2024-05-14T18:14:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if audio.timestamp.corrected_output_device is in the property_contexts as audio_config_prop, does it work?\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/sepolicy/private/property_contexts;drc\u003d5c5ff28912ba4001f48589e88a7f13f25a9989e3;l\u003d399",
      "revId": "2b12aae043b594f91cd474cb516cfff4768f99f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18405c2d_d66d0c14",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-14T20:19:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this property needs to be configurable by vendor, it can be made a \"system internal\" property which means, it can be set from the `system_ext` partition, which is controlled by the vendor. At some point, I have defined `system_audio_config_prop` property context, and the audio server can access it: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/sepolicy/private/property_contexts;l\u003d429;drc\u003d5c5ff28912ba4001f48589e88a7f13f25a9989e3. When performing CTS testing, GSI only provides the system partition, leaving system_ext from the vendor-provided image: https://source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/partitions/shared-system-image\n\nI think, this is more straightforward approach, unless the vendor needs to set the value of this property on a device by device basis.",
      "revId": "2b12aae043b594f91cd474cb516cfff4768f99f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47144b90_9baf00e4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2007245
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-15T01:54:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the explaination. But unfortunately, according to the latest GSI Build 11670440 (released on Apr 4, 2024), the /syste_ext is a link to /system/system_ext, all the changes we made on /system_ext won\u0027t be applied when running CTS-on-GSI. Therefore we came out this approach to take vendor settings affect on GSI.",
      "parentUuid": "18405c2d_d66d0c14",
      "revId": "2b12aae043b594f91cd474cb516cfff4768f99f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b3a517d_1dd4dd47",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-15T21:17:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Steven, you are right. I misunderstood the use of `system_ext`.\n\nIf I understand it correctly, this property needs to be set by the vendor, and then it is read by the system. According to the guide (https://source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/configuration/add-system-properties), it\u0027s a `system_vendor_config_prop`. The audio system already seems to have this kind of properties for AAudio:\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/sepolicy/private/property_contexts;l\u003d1227;drc\u003d1a3775bbb8c9d50a0ffdd944a2dd3d5fbfc4b262\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/sepolicy/public/property.te;l\u003d138;drc\u003d3458c57e5a59c119784597d56c606debcdefce26\n\nSo we can change `audio.timestamp.corrected_output_device` to be a `system_vendor_config_prop`.\n\nI\u0027m curious where `persist.audio.timestamp.corrected_output_device` is currently defined? It seems to me that it should be classified similarly, and it\u0027s also persistent—I suppose these should be thoroughly reviewed.",
      "parentUuid": "47144b90_9baf00e4",
      "revId": "2b12aae043b594f91cd474cb516cfff4768f99f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4b0db4b_91e54e32",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 2007245
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-16T12:29:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you understand correctly, the property needs to be set by the vendor and is read by the system.\n\nWe have a similar approach at https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/system/sepolicy/+/3067142. Setting audio.timestamp.corrected_output_device to aaudio_config_prop also needs to modify prebuilts/api/34.0/private/property_contexts but we are not sure if it\u0027s suitable to do so.\n\nIf we can set audio.timestamp.corrected_output_device directly at vendor, we don\u0027t have to use the persist property anymore.",
      "parentUuid": "1b3a517d_1dd4dd47",
      "revId": "2b12aae043b594f91cd474cb516cfff4768f99f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
